# Solo Dev Hub — global AI rules

This section is managed by Solo Dev Hub. It describes **formats and contracts** used across every project. For per-project context (name, repos, microservices) see the repo's own `CLAUDE.md`.

**Escape rules (apply to all pipe-separated formats below — todo, done, bug-reports):**
- Literal `|` inside a free-form field (`description`, `comment`, `version`) → write as `\|`
- Literal newline inside a free-form field → write as `\n`
- Enum and id fields must not contain `|` or newlines.

## Workflow skills (on-demand)

Workflow-heavy rules are not inlined here — they load on demand. In Claude Code they surface automatically as `sdh-*` skills by their description; for any agent, the same content is in each repo's `docs/sdh_skills/*.md`. Read the matching one when the trigger applies:

| When you… | Skill / file |
|---|---|
| author or close an OUTGOING cross-repo REQ (you're asking) | `sdh-cross-repo-req-send` |
| answer a REQ that ARRIVED for you (write a receipt) | `sdh-cross-repo-req-answer` |
| push an unsolicited announcement to a client / parent server | `sdh-cross-repo-announce-send` |
| start an exchange with an EQUAL (client↔client, server↔server, ms↔ms) | `sdh-peer-channel-send` |
| answer something an equal sent you (ack / handoff / note) | `sdh-peer-channel-answer` |
| process announcements that arrived (at session start) | `sdh-cross-repo-announce-read` |
| add/change/remove an api.md endpoint (maintain your contract) | `sdh-api-contract-maintain` |
| check another repo's server surface before a spec | `sdh-api-contract-consume` |
| apply a practices svod that landed in docs/codex/ (you're a consumer) | `sdh-codex-consume` |
| curate your own Codex svod of practices (you're the publisher) | `sdh-codex-maintain` |
| document a multi-file/multi-layer feature flow | `sdh-feature-flow-docs` |
| scope a non-trivial task (≥2 decisions / cross-boundary / ≥3 subtasks) | `sdh-phase-workflow` |
